  "id": "zajal_lebanese",
  "name": "Zajal (Lebanese improvised sung-poetry duel)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Strophic poetry in Lebanese colloquial Arabic, improvised and sung by teams of poets who answer one another in verbal jousts before an audience, with a chorus repeating the refrains to frame drum and darbuka. It is on the UNESCO Representative List and is associated with poets such as Zaghloul el-Damour and Moussa Zgheib, whose duels were widely recorded; the riq card stands in for the Lebanese def frame drum.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1960s zajal, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. single lead single track no stacking. riq, Egyptian sombaty canonical mid east darbuka. live tracking. Neumann U47, tube pre, German tube console, vari-mu, passive program EQ. tape 15ips plate reverb hall reverb.",
